        if(i % 2 === 0) {
            if (!regex_Vowel.test(str[i])) {
                return false;
            }
        } else {
            if (!regex_Consonant.test(str[i])) {
                return false;
            }
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

The function isAlternatingVowelConsonant first checks if the input string is empty; if true, it will return null. It then moves to check each character of the string: if the position is even, it checks if the character is a vowel by trying to match it with the vowels pattern; if the position is odd, it checks if the character is a consonant or not. If any of the checks fails, it will return false. If all characters pass the check, it will return true. Also, it is case-insensitive as it changes the input string to uppercase first.

