});
```

3. Listening for Realtime Updates
In order to make our web-app reactive and always in sync with Firestore data, we will add event listeners that trigger every time there is a change in our data. Cloud Firestore's onSnapshot() method allows us to listen for updates in realtime. Here's a script showing how we could do this:

```javascript
db.collection('chores').onSnapshot(snapshot => {
    snapshot.docChanges().forEach(change => {
        if (change.type === 'added') {
            console.log('New Chore: ', change.doc.data());
        }
        if (change.type === 'modified') {
            console.log('Modified Chore: ', change.doc.data());
