Regarding the DBML, it's possible to add additional properties (like ProductName) to the Order class in the DBML designer if you like, but these won't be maintained if you refresh the DBML from the database. Also, these won't help you to remove the dedicated queries for related objects since they're unrelated to the LINQ to SQL mechanism for loading related entities.

